%% Novara — feedback submission flow
%% See docs/Engineering-Bible/04-API.md, 05-Business-Rules.md (rule 8)
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant FE as Feedback.tsx
    participant BE as POST /api/feedback
    participant Lim as feedbackLimiter<br/>(10/hr per userId)
    participant DB as Neon: feedback table
    participant Email as lib/email.ts
    participant Resend as Resend API

    U->>FE: fills subject/description/type,<br/>optional contact email
    FE->>FE: zod validation (client-side)
    FE->>BE: POST /api/feedback + Bearer token
    BE->>BE: requireAuth -> req.userId
    BE->>Lim: check rate limit for req.userId
    alt over limit
        Lim-->>FE: 429 Too many feedback submissions
    else within limit
        BE->>BE: validate type/subject/description length
        BE->>DB: INSERT INTO feedback (...)<br/>status = 'new'
        DB-->>BE: row (id, status, createdAt)
        BE-->>FE: 201 { id, type, subject, status, createdAt }
        FE-->>U: toast "Thanks for the feedback!"
        Note over BE,Resend: Response already sent.<br/>Email is best-effort from here.
        BE->>Email: sendFeedbackNotification(payload)
        alt RESEND_API_KEY not set
            Email->>Email: log warning, skip send
        else key configured
            Email->>Resend: emails.send({ to: FEEDBACK_TO_EMAIL, ... })
            alt Resend API error
                Resend-->>Email: { error }
                Email->>Email: throw -> caught by .catch()<br/>logger.error "Failed to send feedback notification email"
            else success
                Resend-->>Email: sent
            end
        end
    end
    Note over DB: The DB row is never rolled back<br/>regardless of email outcome.
